				1482,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose Enhanced IPC modules and enforce PascalCase struct qualification\n\nRemove the monolithic type definitions previously embedded directly in `Source/IPC/Enhanced/ConnectionPool.rs`, `MessageCompressor.rs`, `PerformanceDashboard.rs`, and `SecureMessageChannel.rs`. This refactor prepares the `IPC::Enhanced` layer for a fine-grained modular structure where specific traits and DTOs (e.g., `PoolConfig`, `Compressor::Struct`) reside in dedicated sub-files, aligning with the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions.\n\nUpdate `Source/IPC/Enhanced/mod.rs` to reference these types using explicit qualification (e.g., `ConnectionPool::Pool::Struct` instead of `ConnectionPool::ConnectionPool`). This resolves symbol shadowing issues caused by module-name/type-name collisions and adheres to the architectural shift towards explicit namespace resolution seen in recent command handler refactorings.\n\nThis change cleans up the current implementation state, allowing the `EnhancedIPCManager` to correctly instantiate its internal components (`Compressor`, `Pool`, `Channel`, `Dashboard`) once the corresponding sub-modules are migrated to their own files.",
			"SHA": "51dd389c370787f41e36f29c4e245375e6d4f620"
		}
